- internal: hot KV (2.5 TB), active model shards (1 TB), system (0.5 TB);
- external: direct rank-local model storage, with the remainder pooled
  across the fleet as a striped model store.

- pair-port rx buffer size (auto-sized at link-up);
- IPv6 address generation mode;
- the pair cable (spark8↔spark9 use a 2 m copper cable, the others 0.5 m);
- the switch breakout leg;
- NVMe model or MRRS;
- PCIe parity bits and VSEC dwords;
- kernel 1029;
- sysctls;
- switch-side PFC pause counts.

- one 100 Gb/s port on the CRS804 switched all-to-all fabric (rail 1);
- one 100 Gb/s port on the `cisco0` switched all-to-all fabric (rail 2). The
  direct `rank XOR 1` links are gone since 2026-11-06; rail 2 still reaches
  the partner, now through the switch ([FLEET_FABRIC.md](https://github.com/sparkpipe/datacenter/blob/main/network/FLEET_FABRIC.md));
- 128 GB unified memory;
- one 4 TB internal NVMe; and
- at least one 4 TB external NVMe.

This endpoint already exists in the gateway; OpenAI-compatible tools and SDKs use it. It gains:
- `usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens`;
- the alias and pack names;
- keep-alive comments;
- replay per §3.2.
